  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "there are some issues with parent constraints how they are rendered in vrchat. when in specific configurations ( like hand root and then reparent from hand to waiste ) tends to make it shake around in all configs. after some testing putting it in the hips and then parenting it with the parent constraint to other places does work. but it still is buggy. it still likes to shake around somewhat slightly. and when introducing dynamic bones it really shakes around when waving your hand around. wich is even worse in earlier mentioned configurations setups wich do shake in mirror and other cameras too ( if remmebering correctly )\nwhen in vr it seems to shake around in the personal view. but when looking in the vrc camera. or in the mirror. it doesnt do it. since im thinking those are locally rendered instances, when the POV is instead handling it in the cloud (just a guess) or with some delay between it not rendering it locally it. \nif the way its rendered locally in the mirror and screenshot camera id suggest making the parent constraints rendered locally for the headset POV of the wearer aswell. since they have already got the values to tell em where to go ( if setup right thats a whole bug on its own ) it should work fine as a solution. if the non local rendering is the case.\nive got a setup avatar id that can be tried for it that should produce the same effect as on the model i discovered it with. if needing to record video clips or any other material i should be able to provide it. \nPublic Test Avatar ID: avtr_4f66fb9f-284b-4239-8b56-098223097b65",
